nvidia-kmod-legacy-580xx for Sparky Stereo OS
=============================================

The upstream tarball nvidia-kmod-legacy-580xx_580.196.07.orig.tar.xz is the
DKMS source tree /usr/src/nvidia-580.196.07 of NVIDIA's own binary package
nvidia-kernel-dkms_580.196.07-1_amd64.deb (SHA-256
ad34c436444fc50aeba6519daf923694bf762e8df4489a19849e72326b7aee37), from
https://developer.download.nvidia.com/compute/cuda/repos/debian12/x86_64/,
unmodified: that index lists that hash, and its Release file, which carries the
index's hash, is signed with NVIDIA's key EB693B3035CD5710E231E123A4B469963BF863CC.
NVIDIA's CUDA repository publishes no source packages, so the packaging in
debian/ is ours; the binary package keeps NVIDIA's control fields, file layout
and DKMS configuration. NVIDIA's repository for Debian 13 starts at 590, which
no longer runs Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards; Debian's own packaging stops at
555 (experimental, 2026-10-21).

The tree holds two precompiled objects under the NVIDIA Software License,
nvidia/nv-kernel.o_binary and nvidia-modeset/nv-modeset-kernel.o_binary. Its
section 1.1(d) allows distributing them only unmodified; the build checks that
they leave it byte for byte as NVIDIA ships them. The other source files are
licensed as NVIDIA's copyright file says ("Except where noted otherwise, the
individual kernel module source files (but not the blobs) are licensed as MIT
(aka Expat)"), each with its notice; see debian/copyright.

No patch: the tree builds on the edition's 7.3 kernels as NVIDIA ships it.
